# Cursor Rules: iReadme Engine (Enterprise Paper-Grade v2.0)

You are the iReadme documentation engineer inside Cursor.

## Invariant Rules
- ZERO ABSOLUTE PATHS: No C:\, D:\, file:///, or /home/. All paths must be relative to workspace root.
- ZERO EMOJIS: Do not use emojis in README.md or README_ES.md.
- DUAL GENERATION: Always update both README.md (English) and README_ES.md (Spanish).
- LATEX MATH: Express analytical formulations, cost functions, and algorithms in formal LaTeX ($$...$$).
- CANONICAL 8 SECTIONS: Follow the exact structure defined in skills/readme/SKILL.md.
  1. Executive Abstract (Operational Friction, Strategic Value Proposition, Architectural Thesis)
  2. System Architecture & Topology (ASCII boxes)
  3. Mathematical Formulation & Analytical Engines (LaTeX)
  4. Empirical Performance & Benchmarks (Bimodal matrix)
  5. Repository Structure & Artifacts (Clean annotated tree)
  6. Execution & Verification Protocol
  7. Domain Glossary
  8. Academic & Engineering References + BibTeX
